.th CNVTWTMP VIII 23/3/78
.sh NAME
cnvtwtmp \*- convert old format login history to AUSAM format
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd cnvtwtmp
[-] { used as a filter }
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Cnvtwtmp
converts the old format
.it wtmp
file to the new format as used by AUSAM.
It reads the old passwd file to find user id.s.
The optional argument suppresses warnings
(\ on file 2\ )
which tend to be copious as there were no interlocks on the writing of
.it wtmp
\*.
.sh FILES
/etc/passwd
.sh "SEE ALSO"
AUSAM(VIII), ac(VIII), wtmp(V).
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
yes.
.sh AUTHOR
Piers Lauder (\ University of Sydney\ )
.sh BUGS
